  "contract": [
    "Internal SYSTEM::FUNCTION-LAMBDA-LIST and SYSTEM::OPERATOR-LAMBDA-LIST return a copied list and a separate availability flag. NIL,T means no arguments; NIL,NIL means unavailable.",
    "Retains lambda lists only. Default forms are not evaluated; lexical values and function bodies are not exposed. One generated reader is shared across closures from each source lambda.",
    "Function aliases retain their own definition metadata after redefinition. Macro source lists survive expansion, COMPILE and compiled-file reload; replacing a macro expander clears stale metadata.",
    "Generic-function readers reflect its declared signature, including changes after creation. TRACE wrappers preserve underlying metadata.",
    "Native functions, special operators and compiler transforms without recorded information remain unavailable; their signatures are not guessed.",
    "Target DEFPACKAGE establishes its package and options at compile time and reload. IN-PACKAGE resolves before assigning either package variable, so a missing package does not corrupt compiler state."
  ],
